# Quick Start Guide

## Initialize Project

Initialize from repository root:

```bash
bash init.sh
```

The initializer asks for a few simple values and creates `buildPDF` in project root.

## Build Your Presentation

Build the image once:

```bash
docker pull registry.gitlab.com/woofi4/public/pandoc-presentation-creator/beamer-full:latest
```

Run this command to build your slides:

```bash
docker run --rm \
  -v "$(pwd):/data" \
  --entrypoint=/bin/sh \
  -e INPUT_FILE=/data/slides/Example.md \
  -e OUTPUT_FILE=/data/output/presentation.pdf \
  registry.gitlab.com/woofi4/public/pandoc-presentation-creator/beamer-full:latest \
  -c "/data/buildPDF"
```

## Output

Your presentation will be generated as: `output/presentation.pdf`

## Editing

1. **Edit content**: Modify `slides/Example.md` with your content
2. **Change settings**: Update `config/config.yaml` (defaults) and `config/metadata.yaml` (title, author, date, etc.)
3. **Rebuild**: Run the build command above

## Available Docker Images

- `registry.gitlab.com/woofi4/public/pandoc-presentation-creator/beamer-full:latest` - For PDF (Beamer) output
- `pandoc-revealjs:latest` - For HTML (Reveal.js) output

## Advanced Usage

### Custom Output Name

```bash
docker run --rm \
  -v "$(pwd):/data" \
  --entrypoint=/bin/sh \
  -e INPUT_FILE=/data/slides/Example.md \
  -e OUTPUT_FILE=/data/output/my-presentation.pdf \
  registry.gitlab.com/woofi4/public/pandoc-presentation-creator/beamer-full:latest \
  -c "/data/buildPDF"
```

### Multiple Input Files

#### Adding them separately

```bash
docker run --rm \
  -v "$(pwd):/data" \
  --entrypoint=/bin/sh \
  -e INPUT_FILE=/data/slides/intro.md \
  -e OUTPUT_FILE=/data/output/full-presentation.pdf \
  -e DEFAULTS_FILE=/data/config/config_2.yaml \
  registry.gitlab.com/woofi4/public/pandoc-presentation-creator/beamer-full:latest \
  -c "/data/buildPDF"
```

Note: `buildPDF` supports one markdown input per run. For merged multi-file output, concatenate files first or run pandoc manually.

#### Using a wildcard

##### Linux

```bash
docker run --rm \
  -v "$(pwd):/data" \
  --entrypoint=/bin/sh \
  registry.gitlab.com/woofi4/public/pandoc-presentation-creator/beamer-full:latest \
  -c "/data/buildPDF"
```

##### Windows

```powershell
docker run --rm `
  -v "${PWD}:/data" `
  --entrypoint=/bin/sh `
  registry.gitlab.com/woofi4/public/pandoc-presentation-creator/beamer-full:latest `
  -c "/data/buildPDF"
```

### Override Metadata

```bash
docker run --rm \
  -v "$(pwd):/data" \
  --entrypoint=/bin/sh \
  -e INPUT_FILE=/data/slides/Example.md \
  -e OUTPUT_FILE=/data/output/presentation.pdf \
  -e METADATA_OVERRIDES="title=My Custom Title" \
  registry.gitlab.com/woofi4/public/pandoc-presentation-creator/beamer-full:latest \
  -c "/data/buildPDF"
```

### Add Custom Defaults

Create `config/custom.yaml`:

```yaml
metadata:
  title: "My Custom Presentation"
  institute: "University of Vienna"
```

Run with:

```bash
docker run --rm \
  -v "$(pwd):/data" \
  --entrypoint=/bin/sh \
  -e INPUT_FILE=/data/slides/Example.md \
  -e OUTPUT_FILE=/data/output/presentation.pdf \
  -e DEFAULTS_FILE=/data/config/custom.yaml \
  registry.gitlab.com/woofi4/public/pandoc-presentation-creator/beamer-full:latest \
  -c "/data/buildPDF"
```

### Useful Script Options

- `INPUT_FILE`: markdown input path inside container (default: `/data/slides/Minimalist.md`)
- `OUTPUT_FILE`: output PDF path inside container (default: `/data/output/presentation.pdf`)
- `METADATA_FILE`: pandoc defaults YAML path (default: `/data/config/config.yaml`)
- `DEFAULTS_FILE`: additional defaults YAML path
- `METADATA_OVERRIDES`: space-separated `key=value` pairs
- `PDF_ENGINE`: optional PDF engine override

### Windows Note (`file not found`)

If scripts fail on Windows with `file not found`, normalize line endings:

```bash
git add --renormalize .
```

Then commit changes. `.gitattributes` already enforces LF for shell scripts.

